WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.750
In May 2024, in Iceland, a plant
called Mammoth was switched on.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.130
It pulls CO₂ straight out of the air,

3
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.750
and runs on geothermal energy.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.050
The captured gas is pumped underground,
where it reacts with basalt and turns

5
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.210
to stone.

6
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.510
The company says it is designed to
capture up to 36,000 tonnes a year.

7
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.330
Could machines like it
clean up our emissions?

8
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.830
Would a few dozen do?

9
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.070
Or should we dim the Sun?

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.330
In this mission, you'll see
how carbon pricing works,

11
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.130
from the EU's cap and trade
to China's national scheme.

12
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.990
Then you'll test forest offsets, and
weigh two kinds of geo-engineering.

13
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: decide whether machines
like Mammoth could clean up our emissions.
